#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:20
msgid "Read this before you decide it is not for you"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:22
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Adding a format looks like it should require understanding the engine. It"
" does not, and that is a design decision rather than a happy accident: "
"formats live outside the engine precisely so that the people who know "
"what a fund report *means* do not have to know how a PDF is taken apart "
"({doc}`../../../reference/design/formats-as-plugins`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:27
msgid ""
"Concretely, what a simple format costs is **one row in a spreadsheet**. "
"Here is a real one, the whole extraction configuration for a Luxembourg "
"fund report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:35
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Those trailing numbers are column positions in the report's table, and "
"there is a command that prints the table with its columns numbered so "
"that you can read them off. That is the level of difficulty we are "
"talking about. {doc}`first-format` does exactly this row, from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:39
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Some reports are genuinely awkward, and for those you can drop to writing"
" Python — but you drop only the one segment that needs it, and you keep "
"inheriting the rest ({doc}`../writing-a-format`). Nobody starts there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:43
msgid "The three habits that save the most time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:45
msgid ""
"**Get classification right before anything else.** Which pages the engine"
" even looks at is decided first, and everything downstream is meaningless"
" until it is right. Debugging the extraction of a page that was never "
"selected is the classic way to lose an afternoon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:49
msgid ""
"**Let the tool tell you which segment is wrong.** A page goes through "
"three stages and you can print the output of each one. *\"The page is "
"wrong\"* has no handle on it; *\"the second stage dropped these rows\"* "
"has one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/index.md:53
msgid ""
"**Look at what you are about to freeze.** `make-tests` records what the "
"code does *right now*. Read its output before confirming: a wrong result "
"you confirm becomes the specification, and from then on the test defends "
"the bug."
msgstr ""

